ion when parsing deeply nested arrays) is fixed in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0. I first tried 2.9.4 as the smaller upgrade, but the approver turned that commit down. They said the fastjson 3.x migration was finished last sprint, so I used 3.1.0.\n- **Branch:** `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-3.1.0` updates `requirements.txt` and adds a security entry to `CHANGELOG.md`. An unused branch, `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4`, was left over from the first try and has no new commits. You can delete it.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 597dec07c7.\n- **PR:** When I opened the PR, the response showed no reviewers attached, so I added alex separately.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}